# Start the battery watcher when a Logitech hidraw node appears, at boot too
# (systemd-udev-trigger replays every device). The parent's kernel name is
# bus:vendor:product.id in upper-case hex, the same vendor find_hidpp_nodes in
# peripheral-battery takes from HID_ID, on any bus. The watcher itself tells
# which of these nodes speak HID++; nodes it does not use cost it nothing.
ACTION!="remove", SUBSYSTEM=="hidraw", SUBSYSTEMS=="hid", KERNELS=="*:046D:*", TAG+="systemd", ENV{SYSTEMD_WANTS}+="thinfloe-peripheral-battery-watch.service"
